   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 289 of the laws of 2021 amending the public health law\nrelating to the provision of certain professional services to children's camps\nand camps for children with developmental disabilities, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8403",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8403-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 54,
       "fullName": "Pamela Helming",
       "imgName": "773_Pamela_Helming.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 951,
       "sessionMemberId": 1812,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "HELMING"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 289 of 2021",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8403\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 289 of the laws of 2021 amending the public\nhealth law relating to the provision of certain professional services to\nchildren's camps and camps for children with developmental disabilities,\nin relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo change the effective date of Chapter 289 of 2021, from one year after\nthe bill shall become a law to June 1, 2022.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends section 4 of chapter 289 of the laws of\n2021 amending the public health law relating to the provision of\nservices to children's camps and camps for children with disabilities,\nto make the effective date immediate.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 289 of the Laws of 2021, amending the public health law, author-\nizes the operators of a children's camps and camps for children with\ndisabilities to employ or contract with additional licensed profes-\nsionals to work at the camp.  This chapter does not take effect until\nJuly 16, 2022, which is several weeks into the camp summer season. In\norder to implement this provision, camps will need to hire these profes-\nsionals before summer camp season begins. Accordingly, this bill changes\nthe effective date from one year after the chapter became law (July 16,\n2022) to June 1, 2022. This will ensure that camps have sufficient time\nenough to hire these much-needed licensed professionals for this\nsummer's camp season.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.   \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
